WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.709
Film Courage: Ravi, you were an investment
banker or you did something with finance?

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:04.480
Ravi Patel, Actor: I was!

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.600
I was doing my parent’s dreams.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.950
I did finance and I was working in the banking
world.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:11.950
Film Courage: And what happened?

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:12.950
Ravi: I blew it!

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:18.000
No…I’ll tell you what happened…I got
laid off around 2001 and I’d already used

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.039
up my vacation days.

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:22.050
I new…I was just a horrible investment banker.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.630
I hated it.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.900
Film Courage: Why?

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.720
Ravi: I knew at that point in my life that
I had to at least try something that I cared

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.110
about and that began the journey of me kind
of like spending a your doing a lot of crazy

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:41.330
stuff and eventually after awhile I was in
LA bartending, I was thinking about going

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:47.340
to Law School and I got asked to do an audition
and the next thing you know I was a full time

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.340
actor.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.340
It was crazy.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.640
Film Courage: So how do your parents feel
about it now if you don’t mind me asking?

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.090
Ravi: My parents love it!

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.750
They’re acting now, too!

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.670
Success is great.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.890
Every parents excited when it’s working.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:05.190
But when I first did it they were super scared
because they are naturally conservative.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:11.040
But now they are literally acting now themselves,
so the tables have turned.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.100
Film Courage: Sure.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.770
Was there a moment where you almost went back
[to the 9-to-5 world]?

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:15.770
I know you said you were laid off?

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:18.920
Ravi: I constantly relapse and say why am
I doing this?

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.870
Because acting is a very abusive relationship,
you really have to know what it is.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:28.521
And I’m also not one of those people (those
rare few) that believe that if you want to

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:31.810
be an actor, that it’s all you need to focus
on.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.670
I actually think to be an actor you need to
have other sources of happiness, other sources

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:40.740
of fulfillment and honestly even other sources
of work and then you can really give yourself

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.740
to acting.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.690
Because what makes acting really hard is when
it gets confused with the career because once

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:50.659
you’re relying on acting for money all the
sudden the desperation works its way into

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:54.890
the audition room and some people never figure
out how to do that.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:02:01.229
It’s a really difficult career path to also
do it in a way where you’re actually able

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:08.470
to enjoy the acting and not be completely
reliant on the end (whether you succeed or

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:12.069
not) in order to be happy.

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:18.920
Because I work a ton and even then it’s
so often a struggle, lots of ups-and-downs.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.030
So I have to remember what it is and what
it means for me.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.260
And at this point I have a wife, I have a
kid.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:29.870
I have other sources of fulfillment and I
also have other sources of income because

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.760
that is the only way that I can be happy with
acting.

